# Form rendering

Use `Form::form()` for a new form and when replacing an older one. The class is `Adlexone\Html\Form`. Pass the card title as the first argument. Do not define a `HEADING` constant, and do not call `buildForm`, `buildStartForm`, `buildFormFieldsGrid`, `buildEndFormWithButtons`, or `buildFormSectionHeading`. Those helpers are gone.

Add form markup in `src/Html/Form.php`. Add cards and lists in `src/Html/Blocks.php`. Put the finished HTML on the page with `Page::current()->setBody()`. Page rendering stays in `src/Http/View.php`. List behaviour belongs in `layouts/js/app.js` behind a data attribute. Class names stay aligned with `layouts/css/base.css`.

A new plain field type is `FieldControl::register($type, $render)`. Menus stay in the item screen. An application wording prefix is `Wording::register($controllerPrefix, $constantPrefix)`.

## Pattern

1. Build `$fields` as `label => Form::*()` HTML. A hidden field uses an empty label.
2. Build `$buttons` with `Form::button()`.
3. Call `Form::form($title, $actionUrl, $fields, $buttons)`.
4. `Page::current()->setBody($html)`.

`Form::form()` returns HTML. It does not set the page body.

Field helpers: `text`, `textarea`, `select`, `password`, `checkbox`, `radio`, `hidden`, `file`, `date`, `time`, `datetime`, `email`, `number`, `url`.

## Exemplar

`FieldsScreen::showSearchOptions()` in `src/Screen/FieldsScreen.php`.
